## Performance evidence

**Do not claim a performance fix without a measured before/after number** from the same machine and
session. Before choosing a candidate, read [`optimization-loop-rejections.md`](../issue-handoff/optimization-loop-rejections.md);
skip anything listed unless its "do not retry unless" condition is met.

### Lessons from rejected candidates

- **Measure the step's share of end-to-end time first.** A 1.25x win on a step that is 1% of the call
  is invisible (`_signed_clearance`, ring area/centroid).
- **Fewer calls is not less wall time.** Removing one transform call per point made RC2 605-606 refine
  12.9% slower by median. Call counts are not evidence.
- **NumPy loses on small inputs.** Fixed overhead (~12 µs) plus tuple-to-array conversion (`np.asarray`
  ~95 ns/point) beat a Python loop on rings of tens to hundreds of points.
- **Synthetic-only evidence is not acceptable.** Use `TESTINPUTPATH` fixtures or real volume sizes.

### Required evidence

- pyperf old and new runs to separate JSON under `TESTOUTPUTPATH`, then
  `python -m pyperf compare_to old.json new.json --table`; thresholds in the improve-loop [gates](../skills/nornir-improve-loop/gates.md).
- An **old-vs-new equivalence test** (bit-identical or a stated tolerance) alongside the benchmark.
- **pyperf on Windows:** workers get a stripped environment and cannot import the venv; pass `--copy-env`
  (e.g. `python benchmarks/bench_publish_shared_tiles.py --copy-env -p 10 -o out.json`).
- Pipeline paths (refine, assemble, Pyre registration): PhaseProfiler or medians of repeated runs.

